+ * i.e. a fresh instance of the exact fault we are chasing. Bit 32 already
+ * proved the reset is not the trigger (skipping it still died), so it stays
+ * inline. Only phy_exit() - the clk_bulk_disable_unprepare +
+ * regulator_bulk_disable half, which touches no registers and is safe to run
+ * late - gets deferred.
+ */
